# s5_per_layer: convert, encrypt, move and run one sub-model at a time. Phase B.
#
# pool       after s4_param_defer:
#              W_vram   2.08     peak   362,496 kB    down 19.2x from the baseline's 6,971,392
#              W_host  13.17     peak 2,924,220 kB    down 1.0% from 2,952,288, i.e. never attacked
#            rule 3 -> host.
# object     s4 host table:
#              870.5 MB  29.1%  heap:python3.10+0xd6be1
#              799.0 MB  26.7%  heap:libstdc++.so.6.0.29+0xf3269
#              433.3 MB  14.5%  file:db5325...        mapped; excluded from W by policy, not targetable
#              366.8 MB  12.3%  anon:[heap]           located but unnamed, not targetable
#            top two (55.8%) = whole-model ONNX conversion (Python graph + protobuf).
# donor      SHAFT-CPU s6_per_layer: 2,056,996 -> ~1,290,000 kB; three lifetime releases during
#            conversion (433 MB each) had moved nothing there.
# phase B    (a) transcript summed over 14 sub-graphs (bert_perlayer_gpu.py) must equal s4's;
#            (b) equiv_per_layer.py re-run in this image. s0..s4 phase A, this the first phase B row.
# VRAM       also expected to fall (param_defer_gpu over 14 smaller graphs); step judged on host.
# excluded   torch.cuda.empty_cache() between layers (allocator behaviour, not program demand).
# expected   host -35% to -40%, ~1.75 to 1.90 GB; transcript unchanged.
BASELINE_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_gpu.py
SHAFT_SCRIPT=bert_perlayer_gpu.py
SHAFT_LIMB_LOOP=1
SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16
SHAFT_LEVERS=param_spill_gpu,param_defer_gpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_PARAM_SPILL=1 SNNI_SPILL_DIR=/results"
